Disable fork-ts-checker in the web UI build.

The type checker runs in a forked 4GB process that always OOMs: the
`$eventHub: Vue` property declared on the Vue interface in main.ts is
self-referential, which makes type instantiation explode across every
component (8GB is not enough either). It therefore never produced a
single diagnostic, it only burned ~80s of build time.

ts-loader runs with transpileOnly, so the emitted bundle is identical.

diff --git a/komga-webui/vue.config.js b/komga-webui/vue.config.js
index 52e2553d..839385fe 100644
--- a/komga-webui/vue.config.js
+++ b/komga-webui/vue.config.js
@@ -20,6 +20,12 @@ module.exports = {
     },
   },

+  // the type checker OOMs on the self-referential `$eventHub: Vue` declared in main.ts,
+  // so it never produced any result anyway; ts-loader runs with transpileOnly regardless
+  chainWebpack: config => {
+    config.plugins.delete('fork-ts-checker')
+  },
+
   // custom rule for readium and r2d2bc css that needs to be made available, but untouched
   configureWebpack: {
     module: {
